until the falling of the hammer. (E) The auctioneer can increase the bidding price at any time during the auction. (F) If the auction is without reserve, the auctioneer can withdraw the article at any time prior to the fall of the hammer. (G) All bids are final and cannot be retracted under any circumstances.", "mode": "local", "answer": "D. A bidder may retract his bid at any time until the falling of the hammer.", "answer_ms": 423}
